# MobileCraft: Mobile Ergonomics & Motion Rule

> Author: Ananda Azizul Akbar (@Azizulakbar89)

## 1. Thumb-Zone & Touch Targets
- Anchor primary CTAs and key controls in the lower 35% of the mobile viewport.
- Minimum tap target: `44×44pt` (iOS) or `48×48dp` (Android). Pad smaller icons with `hitSlop` or container padding.

## 2. Navigation & Bottom Sheets
- Keep bottom tab bars strictly for switching top-level views, with `64–72px` height and bottom clearance (`pb-1`, `leading-none`) so labels never clip. Hide the bottom tab bar during focused transactional flows (checkout, transfer, booking).
- Keep top headers compact (`<= 56px`). Never stack multiple header rows.
- Use bottom sheets with drag handles and dimmed backdrops instead of browser `alert()`, `confirm()`, or `prompt()`.

## 3. Safe Areas & Virtualized Lists
- Derive safe-area insets dynamically (`useSafeAreaInsets`, `SafeArea`, `safeAreaInsets`, `WindowInsets`). Never hardcode `paddingTop: 44` or `paddingBottom: 34`.
- Use virtualized lists for large datasets (`@shopify/flash-list`, `ListView.builder`, `LazyVStack`, `LazyColumn`).

## 4. Subtle Motion & Haptics
- Use subtle active press feedback (`scale: 0.97` with snappy spring physics) and light native haptics on key interactions.
- Avoid competing looping animations (`animate-pulse` / `animate-bounce`). Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
